    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Matches two ledgers one-to-one on amount, reference and date with tolerances, plus group matches, and lists the unmatched items on each side.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Finance",
    "tags": [
        "reconciliation",
        "bank reconciliation",
        "matching",
        "accounts payable",
        "accounts receivable",
        "cash",
        "audit",
        "finance",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Matches the items of two ledgers and lists what is left on each side: bank statement against cash book, invoices against payments, a supplier statement against the purchase ledger, card settlements against sales.\n\nMatching runs in passes, each **one-to-one** and best match first:\n\n1. **Exact**: same amount and same reference (references are compared ignoring spaces, punctuation and case), dates within the window\n2. **Amount and date**: amount within the tolerance and dates within the window; the closest date wins, then the closest amount, then a matching reference\n3. **Group**: several items with the same reference that add up to one item on the other side (one payment for three invoices, a deposit banked in two parts)\n\nFields that must agree (account, currency, company) restrict every pass. Side 2 amounts can be **sign-flipped** when one side records credits as negatives.\n\nOutputs: both inputs with match status, match ID and rule, one row per match with the amounts and any difference, and a summary of matched and unmatched items and amounts.",
